+
+`IntervalMatrix::prepare()` borrows an immutable source and records its exact
+singleton-zero coefficients in `PreparedIntervalMatrix`. Repeated `mul_vector`
+and `mul_matrix` calls omit only those zero terms, retaining the original order
+and scalar kernels for every other coefficient. An interval merely containing
+zero is kept. Successful endpoints match the ordinary operations; skipped work
+can let a dyadic query finish under a smaller budget. Dense or small workloads
+can cost more, so preparation is explicit. The view holds inline support flags
+and no scalar copies. Serialize the source and prepare again after validated
+replay; no serialized support mask is accepted as proof.
